g diagonal. Again, good but inferior to winning a piece.\n\nReason: The Black Knight on c5 is a "hanging piece" (undefended and attacked). Capturing it with `P: d4-c5` provides an immediate and significant material advantage (winning a Knight), which is the best way to maximize the probability of winning.\n\nAnswer: P: d4-c5'}
