gical move. It resolves the threat to the c5 pawn by capturing the attacker. It simplifies the position, which is strategically correct when ahead in material. If Black recaptures with the Queen, White can develop the Knight to c3 with tempo. If Black recaptures with the pawn, White maintains a solid position with opened lines for the Rooks.\n\nAnswer: P: c5-d6"}
